<title>MOROCCO: Canada grants $15 mln to Moroccan private sector.</title>
<headline>Canada grants $15 mln to Moroccan private sector.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada granted Morocco $15 million as part of a programme aimed at upgrading the country's private sector, the Moroccan official news agency MAP said on Monday.</p>
<p>Financed by the Canadian Agency for International Development, the package will help small and medium-sized privately-owned firms.</p>
<p>Don Boudria, the Canadian Minister for International Cooperation, and his Moroccan couterpart, Tayeb Fassi Fihri, signed an agreement to implement the project, the agency said.</p>
</text>
